Summary:
During today’s session, we focused on resolving remaining bugs and improving the overall functionality of the Developer Portfolio Evaluator application. Issues identified in previous testing phases were carefully debugged and fixed to ensure smoother performance. In addition to bug fixing, new features were introduced to enhance the evaluation process, including metrics for code quality, project diversity, and hiring readiness. We also implemented a feature to generate a shareable link for the evaluated profile, improving usability and accessibility.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, the application became more feature-rich and reliable with most errors successfully resolved. The newly added evaluation metrics provided deeper insights into a developer’s profile, making the assessment more meaningful. The shareable link functionality improved the practicality of the application for real-world use. Overall, the project evolved into a more comprehensive and user-friendly system with enhanced analytical capabilities.
